# Backend Development Rules

> Canonical, tool-agnostic rules live in [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md).
> Key workspaces: `screener-api/` (main API), `stock-api/` (data services),
> `packages/jobs-runtime/` (jobs runtime & DB access). The original
> `backend/` workspace was deleted from the repo — `screener-api/` is its
> real, current equivalent.

## Directory Structure

```
screener-api/
├── src/
│   ├── core/
│   │   ├── api/           # External API integrations (NSE, BSE, Stockscans auth)
│   │   ├── config/        # Database configuration (Mongo)
│   │   ├── middleware/    # Express middleware (errorHandler, etc.)
│   │   └── utils/         # Utility functions
│   ├── features/          # One folder per feature, each with its own
│   │   │                  # *Routes.js, *Controller.js, and Mongoose models
│   │   ├── stock/
│   │   ├── screener/
│   │   ├── watchlist/
│   │   ├── market/
│   │   ├── orders/
│   │   ├── announcements/
│   │   ├── results/
│   │   ├── admin/
│   │   ├── twitter/
│   │   └── research/
│   └── server.js          # Application entry
└── scripts/                # Data fetching scripts
```

## Adding New API Endpoints

### Step 1: Create Route

```javascript
// screener-api/src/features/newFeature/newFeatureRoutes.js
const express = require('express');
const router = express.Router();
const { handler } = require('./newFeatureController');

/**
 * @route GET /api/new-feature
 * @desc Description of endpoint
 * @access Public
 */
router.get('/', handler);

module.exports = router;
```

### Step 2: Create Controller

```javascript
// screener-api/src/features/newFeature/newFeatureController.js

/**
 * Handler description
 * GET /api/new-feature
 *
 * @see {@link docs/API_REFERENCE.md#new-feature} for API documentation
 */
const handler = async (req, res, next) => {
  try {
    // Implementation
    res.json({ success: true, data: {} });
  } catch (error) {
    next(error);
  }
};

module.exports = { handler };
```

### Step 3: Register Route in server.js

```javascript
app.use('/api/new-feature', require('./features/newFeature/newFeatureRoutes'));
```

### Step 4: Add Tests

```javascript
// screener-api/src/features/newFeature/__tests__/newFeatureController.test.js
// Follow testing conventions in docs/TESTING.md
```

### Step 5: Update Documentation

- Add endpoint to `docs/API_REFERENCE.md`
- Update `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` if needed

## Mongoose Model Template

```javascript
// screener-api/src/features/newFeature/NewModel.js
const mongoose = require('mongoose');

/**
 * NewModel Schema
 */
const newModelSchema = new mongoose.Schema({
  field: {
    type: String,
    required: true,
  },
  createdAt: {
    type: Date,
    default: Date.now,
  },
});

// Indexes
newModelSchema.index({ field: 1 });

module.exports = mongoose.model('NewModel', newModelSchema);
```

